d the full 19-transaction set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Add Transaction form's Description and Amount inputs are HTML5 required fields; submitting empty shows native validation message \\\"Please fill out this field.\\\" and blocks submission (dialog remains open, no new row added).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid date range (start > end) is not rejected or explained\", \"actual\": \"Set From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-01-01 (start later than end). The app did not reject the input or show any explanation of an invalid range; it silently accepted the values and displayed a generic 'No transactions found - Try adjusting your filters' empty state, giving no indication that the date range itself is invalid.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing category is not blocked or identified\", \"actual\": \"Submitted the Add Transaction form with Description and Amount filled but Category left as \\\"Select category\\\" (unselected). The transaction was created successfully with a blank category (table row shows empty Category cell) instead of being rejected with a validation message.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting an in-use category is not blocked and does not require reassignment\", \"actual\": \"Deleted the 'Interest Income' category which had 1 assigned transaction (tx-9, Bank Interest). Confirmation dialog only warned 'Transactions using this category will not be deleted' with no reassignment step. After confirming, transaction tx-9's Category cell became blank instead of showing 'Unknown' or being reassigned/blocked.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding a current-month (Aug 25 2026) income transaction of $555.55, Dashboard Monthly Income updated from $0 to $556, Net Profit/Loss updated from $0 to $556, and Recent Transactions list immediately showed the new transaction at top - all without page reload.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After unmarking tax-related, 2026 Tax Summary showed $0.00 income/0 transactions. After re-marking tax-related on the same transaction, Tax Summary immediately updated to $600.00 income, 1 transaction, with category breakdown 'Sales Revenue $600.00' and the transaction listed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Sales Revenue category count/total updated from 3 transactions/$36,750 to 4 transactions/$37,305.55 immediately after creating a new $555.55 Sales Revenue transaction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked 'Print Report' for year 2026 and year 2024; page remained responsive with no new console errors triggered by the print action itself (window.print() invoked without throwing).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table displays Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, and Tax (✓/blank) columns for every row, plus Total Income and Total Expenses summary for the current result set at the bottom of the page.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Reports page for August 2026 shows Income $600, Expenses $0, Profit +$600, Income by Category (Sales Revenue $600), matching the single Aug 2026 transaction. Dashboard Monthly Income/Profit ($600) and Recent Transactions also match underlying transaction data.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision for values below $1,000 (including below $500)\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard 'Income vs Expenses' chart Y-axis, with an actual data point of $600 (August), shows tick labels ['$0k','$0k','$0k','$0k','$1k'] - four of the five ticks display as '$0k' even though they represent distinct non-zero values (e.g. $150, $300, $450), making them indistinguishable from zero on the axis.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
